1.5.evidence:
Article 7
(1) The implementation of Protection for female Workers/Laborers is realized by preventing acts of economic exploitation and cruel and inhumane treatment and by pursuing appropriate recognition for work performed by women.
(2) Female Workers/Laborers as referred to in paragraph (1) receive protection for:
a. recognition of rights, wages, and decent working conditions;
b. health insurance and social security for employment;
c. access to information and legal consultation services;
d. opportunities to obtain knowledge and skills to improve status; and
e. violence in the workplace.

2.5.evidence:
Article 38
Guidance as referred to in Article 37 paragraph (2) includes: a. providing socialization to the Community and business sector regarding policies on protection and Empowerment of Women;
b. providing books, leaflets, brochures regarding protection and Empowerment of Women, and other related issues as well as disseminating them to the Community;
c. facilitation..................
